From 912eaa1b97a02cf28d3e9e26bd95a3776cc6db00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: beau4201 <beau.ten.berge@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:04:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] oblivios: the cold duress unlock at about 0.90 s, its start
 order, home start and exit

Squash of former patches:

- 0026 oblivios: start the decoy home after the keyguard has gone away and hold the going-away until the user change is applied
- 0027 oblivios: request the exit of an authorized switch as soon as the switch is released and keep the ordinary unlock animation
- 0028 oblivios: do not wait for the decoy's unlock to finish before the duress switch, and start its home 150 ms after the going-away
- 0029 oblivios: a global setting turns the fast duress unlock off for a comparison, consume the home deferral with every switch
- 0030 oblivios: post the deferred decoy home start only when one is waiting, so an ordinary unlock posts nothing
- 0031 oblivios: copy the owner's Auto confirm unlock to the decoy at the lock when both PINs have the same length
- 0032 oblivios: keep the notification stack hidden when the bouncer-to-gone transition ends during an authorized switch
- 0033 oblivios: log the hold and release of the exit and the deferral of the home for the timing rows
- 0034 oblivios: the stage logs of the fast switch exist on debuggable builds only
- 0035 oblivios: copy the owner's wallpaper files to the decoy instead of setStream, which never finished for a user that is not on screen
- 0036 oblivios: do not kill the decoy's packages at the start of the switch back, its home is the stage of the exit
