+ * ObliviOS: copies the owner's wallpaper files to the decoy user's, file by file.
+ *
+ * <p>The wallpaper service keeps four image files and one metadata file per user in that user's
+ * system directory (WallpaperUtils): the source image and its crop for the home screen, the same
+ * pair for a separate lock screen wallpaper, and wallpaper_info.xml, which names the component, the
+ * crop and the colours. A copy through WallpaperManager#setStream only writes the source image: the
+ * service finishes such a set (the crop, the metadata, the binding) in a file observer that it
+ * starts for the current and for an unlocked user only, so for the decoy, which is neither while the
+ * owner is on screen, the set was never finished and its home screen stayed black (lynx
